{{Interlanguage link|{{PAGENAME}}|simple||ja|水若酢神社|zh|水若酢神社}} is [[Shinto shrine|a Shinto shrine]] located in [[Oki District, Shimane|Oki District, Shimane]]. It is a [[Myojin Taisha|Myojin Taisha]]. It is also the [[Ichinomiya]] [[Oki Province]] or the highest ranked shrine in the province.. It is now a [[Beppyo shrine]] . The crest of the shrine has a chrysanthemum symbol".<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-05-28 |title=水若酢神社（Mizuwakasu Shrine） - shrine-heritager |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528184043/https://shrineheritager.com/en/%E6%B0%B4%E8%8B%A5%E9%85%A2%E7%A5%9E%E7%A4%BE%EF%BC%88mizuwakasu-shrine%EF%BC%89/ |access-date=2023-11-21 |website=web.archive.org}}</ref>

It enshrines the deity responsible for the development of the land of [[Oki]], a deity that provides protection at sea.<ref>{{Cite book |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=JSMvAAAAYAAJ&newbks=0&printsec=frontcover&dq=Mizuwakasu&q=Mizuwakasu&hl=en |title=Shinto shrines and festivals |date=1958 |publisher=Association of Shinto Shrines, Kokugakuin University, Institute for Japanese Culture and Classics |language=ja}}</ref>

In the [[Engishiki Jinmyocho]] it is a [[Myojin Taisha]].<ref>{{Cite book |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=QmdRAAAAYAAJ&newbks=0&printsec=frontcover&dq=Mizuwakasu&q=Mizuwakasu&hl=en |title=Engi-shiki; Procedures of the Engi Era: Books VI-X |date=1972 |publisher=Sophia University |language=en}}</ref>

